ast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Carolina remains one of the closest battlegrounds in presidential politics, and the 2028 race opens with no clear favorite. The state has tilted narrowly Republican in recent cycles, with a partisan lean of about one point to the right of the nation, but its margins have been consistently tight. No public general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, and neither side has a defined nominee or fundraising record to assess.\n\nWith so little race-specific information, expectations rest on the state's fundamentals: a slight Republican edge in a state that has decided presidential elections by low single digits. Uncertainty is correspondingly wide, and a modest shift in the national environment, turnout, or the candidates who ultimately emerge could easily move North Carolina to either column.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4508, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4639, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4659, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4636, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4637, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4628, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4642, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4617, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4598, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4577, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4622, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.4697, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.4532, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4593, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4623, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.4753, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.4625, "margin": -1.0}, {"da